  "question": {
    "text": "<p>If the coefficient of friction between the wedge&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and block&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;shown in the figure is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi></math>,&nbsp;then the maximum possible horizontal acceleration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;for which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;doesn&#39;t slip is [angle of inclination of wedge =&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>]</p>\r\r<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0107_29a8b0d470af.jpg\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 122px;\" /></p>\r"
  },
